# Movable HUD implementation checklist

Source proposal: [MovableHudProposal.md](MovableHudProposal.md)
Parent task: [project.todo](../project.todo), HUD Indicators.

## Goal and scope

Make registered HUD indicators and their groups movable through hover controls, with native coordinate persistence and snapping-created arbitrary groups. Keep feature overlays/presentations responsible only for readings, measurements, visibility, and drawing. Reuse native HUD/dialog lifecycle, event routing, GUI bounds/scaling, and position storage.

Persist arbitrary membership through a focused layout metadata boundary, reusing native coordinates. Do not add nested groups, an arbitrary inter-group docking graph, or a separate editor window. Unlocked mouse movement editing includes registered hidden indicators through visible placement proxies. Do not rewrite feature registrations or duplicate overlay instances. Built-in placements remain defaults. All tasks below remain unchecked until their stated evidence is available; source/headless results do not establish live interaction quality.

## Assumptions and decisions to resolve

- Use the native titlebar with its native Fixed/Movable dropdown and the approved compact orange skin: 22 GUI units high with localized group captions at normal HUD text size; retain the native dropdown and close controls. Adapt hover visibility, content-origin persistence, and cancellation around the widget; do not substitute a direct mode-toggle interaction.
- Saved positions use native integer GUI-unit X/Y coordinates, not persisted screen-edge anchors or pivots. Explicit membership metadata will distinguish defaults, independent items, and custom groups; coordinate presence alone is insufficient. Client settings apply across worlds.
- Use 16-physical-pixel acquisition, 26-pixel release, and Shift bypass. Valid grouping outranks alignment guides. Within each intent, retain the target/member/side or alignment identity first, then distance and ordinal identity. Alignment-zone hysteresis is min(6 physical pixels, target cross-span / 12); native rounding moves guides to the resolved position within one GUI unit.
- Resolve compact handle dimensions, title/menu presentation, and control-to-content origin mapping in the prototype; do not silently introduce resizing or close-indicator behavior.
- Run build/test tools through subagents as required by repository instructions. Leave live acceptance to the user; do not launch the game automatically.

## Phase 1: Verify one movable group and the native titlebar adapter

Outcome: one existing group can demonstrate hover controls, native persisted dragging, and safe cancellation before individual movement or snapping is built.

- [x] Reconfirm the owning seams in `HudOverlayHost`, `HudOverlayHoverLabels`, `HudOverlaySession`, `HudOverlayGroupLayout`, and native titlebar/composer input routing.
  - [x] Identify how group placement previews enter layout without being overwritten by ordinary per-frame synchronization.
  - [x] Keep the prototype restricted to one existing group, without changing feature overlays or presentation classes.
- [x] Prototype a separate native control composition around `GuiElementDialogTitleBar`.
  - [x] Use a distinct stable VE dialog key and native Fixed/Movable behavior, restore, and release-time persistence.
  - [x] Gate rendering/hit testing to free-cursor hover or active interaction; respect foreground dialogs and global HUD visibility.
  - [x] Keep controls visible while moving from content onto the handle and throughout dragging; place controls above content or below it near the screen edge.
  - [x] Establish consistent control/content origin mapping so moving the handle below the content never changes the saved content position.
  - [x] Route only handle/active-drag input, continue outside initial bounds, and avoid the default dialog methods' whole-composer event consumption.
  - [x] Preserve content measurements, packing, sampling, and prepared artwork while controls appear or positions change.
  - [x] Paint the slim titlebar with radial-menu orange and normal HUD text; keep native menu/close hit geometry aligned with its glyphs.
  - [x] Show a translucent orange panel over exact hovered group bounds behind the content, and an unfilled orange bounds outline whenever the cursor is free and that group is Movable.
- [x] Verify cancellation restores starting placement without committing a position: Escape, cursor capture changes, GUI hiding, world exit, target removal, and loss of active interaction.
- [x] Record the adapter decision with source/headless evidence and user-run interaction evidence.
  - [x] Check native focus management with other dialogs open; `Focusable = false` alone is insufficient.
  - [x] Reuse the actual native titlebar and dropdown while retaining safe content dragging, cancellation, and `GetDialogPosition`/`SetDialogPosition` persistence.
  - [x] Remove the rejected adapter path and temporary prototype-only scaffolding once the retained approach is established.

Completion criteria:

- [x] The retained approach supports one group, native persistence across client restart, reachable hover controls, selective input, and cancellation without a separate persistence system.
- [x] The user has validated the prototype's hover/input behavior, including foreground windows, before expansion to individual containers and snapping.

Completion evidence:

- The retained one-group integration uses the actual native titlebar and Fixed/Movable dropdown with the approved compact orange skin. Separate control bounds preserve content measurements and packing; native settings store the content origin rather than the temporary above/below titlebar origin.
- Source and headless coverage verifies selective input, native dropdown navigation, foreground-window priority, reachable controls, cancellation without persistence, content-origin restoration, resource reuse, and lifecycle cleanup. Appearance is reviewed in game rather than asserted through visual presets.
- The final full suite passed 2,199/2,199 tests with no failures or skips. Receipt: `artifacts/test-results/visual-policy/visual-policy-full.trx` (repository-relative). Second review and the independent completion audit found no remaining required source defect.
- The user previously confirmed dragging and position persistence, and explicitly signed off this prototype by requesting that Phase 1 be marked complete on 2026-10-17. This records acceptance without attributing additional individual live-test observations to the user. No game was launched by the agent.

## Phase 2: Resolve persisted group positions through the shared runtime

Depends on Phase 1. Outcome: every registered group uses a consistent saved/default/preview position with existing packing and native scaling.

- [x] Add focused position integration under `HudOverlays`, keeping file responsibilities separate and session/system composition thin.
  - [x] Assign stable, distinct VE namespaced group and indicator keys without colliding with other dialogs.
  - [x] Read native positions and map valid integer GUI-unit content origins through `HudOverlayPlacement`; missing entries retain registered defaults.
  - [x] Make active drag preview override saved placement and registered defaults, with starting placement retained for cancellation.
  - [x] Apply native coordinate rounding and screen clamping; preserve saved origin through size/style changes, subject to reachability.
- [x] Integrate group placement resolution with `HudOverlaySession`, `HudOverlayGroupLayout`, and scheduler anchor availability.
  - [x] Use the same effective placement for layout and availability; a moved screen-positioned group must not depend on its former native anchor.
  - [x] Preserve internal group packing and update bounds/clips without refreshing readings or allocating feature artwork.
  - [x] Retain saved overrides across unrelated configuration changes; use registered placement again only after reset.
- [x] Generalize the retained hover/drag controls to registered groups and add group-default restoration via clearing their native position keys.
  - [x] Keep input, control composition resources, and preview state owned by the shared host/session runtime and release them safely on teardown/rebinding.
- [x] Add focused verification for key isolation, native position read/write/reset, preview precedence/cancellation, scaling, viewport/style changes, effective-anchor availability, and unchanged packing/content ownership.

Completion criteria:

- [x] All registered groups can use persisted positions and reset to defaults without altering feature registrations or other dialogs' settings.
- [x] Position-only movement neither resamples readings nor recreates feature presentations, and session replacement leaves no retained interaction resources.

Completion evidence:

- Shared session-owned group preferences restore native integer content origins once, with separate group/indicator key namespaces. Active previews override saved/default placement; cancellation discards previews, successful drops use native truncation, and Fixed clears only the selected group key.
- Every registered group uses the retained native hover controls. Layout and scheduler availability both use screen placement for moved groups; saved origins survive configuration, size, and viewport changes while effective bounds remain clamped and packing stays intact. Feature registrations and presentation ownership are unchanged.
- Second review and the independent completion audit found no required unresolved issue. Final production/test build and full suite passed 2,209/2,209; focused HUD coverage passed 265/265, with no failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-phase2/phase2-full.trx` and `phase2-focused.trx` in the same directory (repository-relative). Diff checks are clean.
- Live appearance acceptance remains in Phase 6; no game was launched. Individual containers and snapping remain outside this completed scope.

## Design revision and retained foundation

Completed Phases 1 and 2 establish native controls, group origins, selective input, scaling, and shared availability. Their checkmarks describe that verified foundation, not arbitrary grouping. Remaining work replaces named groups as player-facing destinations with runtime containers created by snapping. Built-in registrations remain initial/reset defaults and retain feature ownership.

The completed foundation's Fixed-to-default reset behavior is superseded by the approved permission-only Fixed mode. Phase 4 must replace that behavior and its tests; the completed evidence above does not establish the revised semantics.

## Approved design contract for remaining work

- Groups are arbitrary, flat runtime containers spanning any registered indicators. Built-in named groups are initial/reset templates, not membership restrictions.
- Mixed arrangements support above/below/left/right attachments with three alignments per side. Pointer position selects alignment and the preview shows the resulting arrangement.
- Native `GuiComposer` and `ElementBounds` remain the composition/geometry foundation; VE resolves attachment relationships and grouping semantics around them.
- Size changes preserve attachment sides, alignment, and gaps by moving connected neighbors. The group top-left origin stays fixed, subject to screen clamping.
- Outside movement editing, hidden members collapse only after their normal transition releases the footprint. During unlocked-mouse editing they use prepared stand-ins without changing normal feature state. Saved membership and attachments remain intact, and space reopens on return. Hiding must not dissolve groups.
- Individual snaps create or join groups. Whole-group snaps merge into groups or independent targets, preserving both internal arrangements in a single flat membership set. Preview before release; cancellation restores both arrangements.
- Fixed targets accept joins/merges and retain Fixed mode. Added content grows the destination toward the attachment, retaining its opposite edge and selected cross-axis anchor; native rounding/clamping may adjust the final origin. Fixed/Movable changes dragging permission only, preserving placement and membership.
- Dragging an individual away ungroups it. One global Reset HUD layout restores all built-in groups/positions, including retained overrides for unavailable integrations. No per-item/group reset or separate ungroup menu is required.
- Native coordinates remain reusable, but explicit versioned membership/layout metadata is required. Select its storage and recovery contract before implementing persistence.

## Phase 3: Resolve arbitrary group semantics and persistence contract

Depends on Phase 2. Outcome: settle the new membership model and storage contract before runtime implementation. The user approved the detailed pair-tree layout and authoritative native JSON snapshot contract on 2026-10-17. Source: [MovableHudProposal.md](MovableHudProposal.md), Placement and group behavior, Native layout reuse assessment, Approved detailed layout contract, Snapping and membership commits, Persistence.

- [x] Incorporate the approved design contract above and resolve only the outstanding design choices with the user before implementing them; do not reopen already approved decisions.
  - [x] Define which snaps create/join groups versus align only, insertion feedback, and Shift bypass.
  - [x] Define the remaining mixed-arrangement semantics: perpendicular insertion. Size changes preserve attachments, alignments, and gaps by repositioning connected neighbors; keep the group top-left origin fixed, subject to screen clamping. Hidden members collapse their space after normal visibility transitions release the footprint, retaining saved membership/attachments and reopening space when visible; temporary hiding must not dissolve groups. All four attachment sides and start/center/end alignment on each side are approved, selected by pointer position with a layout preview. Use the approved native GuiComposer/ElementBounds foundation; settle the VE attachment representation before implementation.
  - [x] Specify the approved global Reset HUD layout action: restore all built-in groups and positions, including unavailable indicators; preserve unrelated settings. No per-item/group reset or separate ungroup menu is required: dragging an individual away ungroups it. Fixed/Movable controls permission only and preserves placement/membership. Fixed targets accept joins and merges while retaining Fixed mode and the opposite outer edge under outward growth, subject to native rounding and screen clamping. Whole-group merging is approved: preserve both internal arrangements, preview the combined result, support Shift bypass, and restore both arrangements on cancellation.
- [x] Define a flat container model with stable opaque group IDs and exactly one container per indicator; built-in names are default templates only.
  - [x] Specify source removal, target insertion, singleton normalization, empty-group cleanup, and temporarily unavailable membership.
  - [x] Define attachment representation, dependency ordering, cycle/conflict handling, and overlap resolution for perpendicular insertions and merges. Distinguish internal layout relationships from prohibited nested player-facing groups or inter-group docking graphs.
  - [x] Define collapse/reappearance through hidden attachment intermediates and branches without deleting saved relationships; count saved members rather than only visible members when deciding singleton/empty cleanup.
  - [x] Define movement-permission ownership for individual grips, independent items, and merged containers, preserving the approved Fixed-target semantics. Fixed locks both group movement and member detachment; overlapping grouping snaps are rejected rather than rearranging existing items. Specify persistence/defaults for this state rather than inferring permission from a saved position.
  - [x] Keep feature registrations and overlay lifetimes unchanged; do not duplicate sampling or drawing ownership.
- [x] Inspect native structured client settings and choose supported metadata persistence or a VE JSON file.
  - [x] Specify versioning, validation, unknown IDs, newly registered IDs absent from a snapshot, duplicate membership recovery, invalid attachment references, offscreen origins, and client-wide behavior across worlds. Preserve temporarily unavailable metadata during loading, migration, and configuration changes.
  - [x] Specify stable, distinct native keys for default containers, custom containers, and independent items. Persist IDs, membership, order, layout policy, and attachment descriptions; do not serialize bounds/composers or encode metadata in fake coordinate keys.
  - [x] Define authority and recoverable commit ordering across metadata and native position writes; previews never persist.
  - [x] Define migration/precedence for existing saved native group origins and global reset behavior, including clearing retained VE overrides for unavailable integrations without touching unrelated settings. Define safe reset of malformed/newer metadata using only provably owned cleanup keys and authoritative initialized reset state.
- [x] Reconcile the chosen decisions into the proposal and remaining tasks before implementation.

Completion criteria:

- [x] Grouping, layout, reset, and persistence decisions are explicit and approved; no runtime policy is inferred from old named groups.
- [x] The model can represent and restore arbitrary groups without nested membership, orphaned items, or loss of unrelated settings.
- [x] The attachment model explicitly covers all approved sides/alignments, resize/collapse behavior, merge preservation, and movement permissions; storage and failure-recovery choices are settled before runtime writes.

Completion evidence:

- The user approved the detailed pair-tree arrangement and authoritative versioned JSON snapshot contract on 2026-10-17, after separately approving rejected overlapping snaps and Fixed locking both group movement and member detachment.
- Proposal sections Approved interaction decisions, Native layout reuse assessment, and Approved detailed layout contract specify flat membership, all attachment sides/alignments, native composition reuse, resize/collapse, create/join/merge/detach, permissions, stable keys, migration, global reset, validation, and interrupted-write recovery. The public ISettings/IGuiAPI/ICoreAPI sources and native bounds/composer implementation were inspected for the storage and layout boundaries.
- The second review and independent completion audit passed after reconciling native coordinates as mirrors rather than the authority. Subsequent implementation/verification tasks reference the approved contract, including newly registered IDs, unavailable members, and malformed/newer metadata reset. Diff checks are clean.
- This is design-contract completion only. No runtime code changed, no build/test run was needed, and later implementation and live acceptance remain unchecked.

## Phase 4: Implement effective containers and individual movement

Depends on Phase 3. Outcome: indicators and groups use resolved membership and cancellable layout transactions.

Source: [MovableHudProposal.md](MovableHudProposal.md), Player interaction, Placement and group behavior, Native layout reuse assessment, Approved detailed layout contract, Persistence, Integration boundaries.

- [x] Resolve default, independent, and custom containers before packing, sharing effective placement with scheduler availability.
  - [x] Remove the layout assumption that every member must share its registered GroupId, while retaining registration identities.
  - [x] Apply the approved group layout policy, size/style repacking, clipping, and native scaling.
- [x] Implement mixed attachment resolution using the approved native composer/bounds foundation.
  - [x] Resolve all four sides and three alignments per side with normal gaps, approved dependency ordering, and cycle/conflict handling. Apply container-local nonnegative GUI-unit rectangles to native bounds before native scaling/clipping.
  - [x] Reuse native hierarchy and alignment where applicable; explicitly recalculate relationships that copy/fixed helpers do not retain. Avoid circular fit-to-children/percentage sizing and do not treat native child fitting as automatic flow/collapse.
  - [x] Preserve attachments and reposition connected neighbors after measured size/style changes, retaining the group top-left origin subject to clamping.
  - [x] Collapse hidden/inapplicable space after visibility transitions release it and reopen it on return, including hidden intermediates/branches. Do not delete membership or dissolve a group because only one member is visible.
  - [x] Update native roots, member bounds, and clips without per-drag `ReCompose`, feature resampling, or feature artwork recreation. Keep feature ownership independent of layout dependencies.
- [x] Add distinct individual and container controls using drawable clipped targets; custom groups need no names.
  - [x] Preserve transient-control measurements, selective input, native menu behavior, and orange hover/movable cues.
  - [x] Keep invisible/reserved/unprepared feature content untargetable while retaining saved membership; unlocked-mouse editing may expose explicit visible placement proxies for registered items.
  - [x] Retain controls during pointer travel and active drags; keep above/below handles reachable at screen edges and independent of content footprints. Preserve foreground/modal priority and dismiss controls without disabling indicators.
- [x] Implement transactional membership/position previews for individual dragging, including ungrouping by dragging away.
  - [x] Preview source removal and repacking; free drops produce independent items.
  - [x] Cancellation restores original container identity, order, membership, and origin without writes.
  - [x] Cover Escape, cursor capture, GUI hiding, target removal, world/session exit, and loss of active interaction; restore source attachment descriptions and movement permission along with placement.
  - [x] Free group movement retains current membership; grouping drops may merge the whole group. Independent items no longer follow former groups.
- [x] Implement approved metadata persistence, migration, recovery, singleton/empty cleanup, and the global Reset HUD layout action. Adapt native Fixed handling to preserve current placement and membership.
  - [x] Implement the approved container-level movement permissions and explicit persisted mode; Fixed locks member detachment as well as group dragging. Replace the foundation's native Fixed callback that clears position keys; mode toggles retain the current origin and membership. Remove superseded partial-reset paths and update their expectations.
  - [x] Global reset restores default templates and positions for all known/retained VE items, including unavailable integrations; subsequent reload must not resurrect cleared custom groups or coordinates.
  - [x] Preserve unknown/unavailable members during ordinary operation; global reset clears all retained VE layout overrides. Always preserve unrelated native dialog settings.
  - [x] Release all interaction/composition resources on removal and session replacement.
- [x] Verify mixed-registration containers, duplicate prevention, independent drawing/updating exactly once, packing, availability, configuration changes, recovery, and lifecycle cleanup.
  - [x] Test every side/alignment with caller-supplied measurements, negative-origin normalization, attachment conflicts, size propagation, retained top-left origin, and screen clamping at multiple GUI scales.
  - [x] Test fade-out then collapse, reappearance through hidden intermediates, all-hidden groups, and true member removal separately from temporary hiding.
  - [x] Test permission-only mode toggles and locked-member detachment, newly registered IDs with existing snapshots, global reset including unavailable entries and malformed/newer metadata, restart/migration precedence, invalid metadata, and recovery at the defined write boundaries. Verify no writes during previews or effective viewport clamping.
  - [x] Verify repeated movement/repacking reuses presentations and cached readings, preserves registered identity, and releases session-owned controls/bounds without disposing feature-owned resources.

Completion criteria:

- [x] Membership resolution drives layout and availability consistently, without changes to feature ownership.
- [x] Successful free drops and explicit membership actions persist; cancellation and failed writes recover according to the approved contract.
- [x] Mixed arrangement, resize/collapse/reappearance, permission-only mode changes, and global reset have focused behavioral evidence using native bounds/composer integration.

Completion evidence:

- Effective containers resolve default templates, independent indicators, and saved mixed-registration pair trees before native layout and scheduler availability. Native roots/members/clips and prepared presentations are reused; hidden branches collapse after transitions release their footprints and reopen without deleting membership.
- Shared native controls provide distinct group/member grips, permission-only Fixed/Movable behavior, transactional detachment/free drops, and global Reset HUD layout. Active member grips survive singleton previews; structural membership keeps group controls distinct when other members are hidden. Cancellation restores the complete prior arrangement without writes.
- The authoritative native JSON snapshot validates membership, stable keys, permissions, layout, and integer origin checkpoints. Legacy migration, successive default remainders, unavailable integrations, reset, mirror failures, ambiguous assignments, and malformed/newer metadata recovery are covered. Precise transient origins are rounded only on commit; effective viewport clamping does not rewrite preferences.
- Second review and the independent completion audit passed after all findings were resolved. Final production/test build and full suite passed 2,250/2,250; focused HUD coverage passed 293/293, with no failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-phase4/phase4-full.trx` and `phase4-focused.trx` in the same directory (repository-relative). Diff checks are clean.
- No game was launched. Native client-restart appearance/interaction acceptance remains in Phase 6; snap-based group creation and merging remain in Phase 5. This completion does not claim those later requirements are implemented or accepted.

## Phase 5: Implement snapping-created groups and previews

Depends on Phase 4. Outcome: individual snaps create/join groups and whole-group snaps merge containers while preserving internal arrangements.

Source: [MovableHudProposal.md](MovableHudProposal.md), Approved interaction decisions, Snapping and membership commits, Persistence.

- [x] Implement geometry-only snap candidates with measured bounds, locality, deterministic tie-breaking, hysteresis, and Shift bypass.
  - [x] Start with a 6-physical-pixel threshold; define the wider release threshold.
  - [x] Derive unsnapped geometry from total pointer delta; exclude the source container/descendants, hidden items, handles, shadows, and tooltips.
  - [x] Distinguish grouping adjacency from screen/edge/center alignment according to the approved policy.
  - [x] Select above/below/left/right attachment and its three cross-axis alignments from pointer position; include side, alignment, target identity, and grouping/alignment-only intent in preview candidates.
- [x] Add a grouping resolver and preview transaction over geometric candidates.
  - [x] An independent target creates a group containing both items; a grouped target receives the new item without nesting.
  - [x] Preview target membership, insertion position, resulting packing, source gap closure, and destination highlight.
  - [x] Use normal gaps and the same resolved mixed layout for preview and commit. Preserve existing internal attachments during whole-group merging rather than flattening geometry into a row or column.
  - [x] Implement approved whole-group merging into a group or independent item, retaining internal arrangements in one flat membership set. Preview the combined layout; Shift bypasses merging and cancellation restores both source and destination. Allow Fixed targets to receive joins/merges without enabling movement; grow toward the incoming item while preserving the opposite outer edge and selected cross-axis anchor, subject to native rounding and screen clamping.
- [x] Render alignment guides and grouping destination/insertion feedback through shared runtime controls, without owning feature textures/state or affecting measured content footprints.
- [x] Reconcile preview geometry with screen clamping and native integer rounding; discard invalid grouping candidates/guides.
- [x] Commit selected membership and placement together through the recovery boundary only after successful release.
  - [x] Shift/free drops preserve independent placement as appropriate; alignment-only snaps never create membership.
  - [x] All cancellation paths restore both source and target arrangements without persistent changes.
  - [x] Do not mutate membership from incidental proximity, screen alignment, or a bypassed/invalid candidate. Do not write metadata or native coordinates on each pointer move, or rebuild feature artwork for previews.
- [x] Verify create/join/leave, whole-group merges and their cancellation, repeated insertion, same-container operations, competing candidates, hidden/removed targets, singleton cleanup, Shift switching, scale conversion, and interrupted commits.
  - [x] Cover every side/alignment for individual and whole-group drops, cross-registration membership, both internal arrangements after merge, and Fixed-target mode preservation and outward-growth edge anchoring.
  - [x] Check deterministic tie-breaking, wider release hysteresis, locality/exclusions, long drags without accumulated error, Shift transitions, and grouping invalidated by clamping/rounding. Guides must describe the final committed geometry.
  - [x] Check membership and origins after restart, failure recovery, and cancellation at all inherited interaction-loss boundaries; prove alignment-only neighbors remain independent.

Completion criteria:

- [x] Snap-created groups persist and move together, with no duplicate membership or nested groups.
- [x] Preview, committed layout, guides, reset, and cancellation obey the approved semantics and survive restart.

Completion evidence:

- Geometry-only candidates use measured visible bounds, 6-pixel acquisition and 10-pixel release hysteresis, deterministic selection, total pointer displacement, and Shift bypass. Individual insertion and whole-tree merging preserve flat membership, destination permission/origin, and existing internal arrangements.
- Shared controls show the resolved destination/insertion layout and alignment guides. Preview and native placement share safe-inset clamping and integer-origin reconciliation; overlaps and unrepresentable guides are rejected. Base/preview compositions are reused during a held drag, with inactive cached geometry excluded from drawing and targeting.
- Membership and origins commit together through the authoritative snapshot boundary. Headless coverage verifies all attachment policies, cross-registration membership, create/join/leave, merge preservation, repeated/same-container insertion, hidden/removed targets, cancellation boundaries, Fixed destinations, Shift transitions, scale conversion, clamping, alignment-only independence, restart reconstruction, reset, and interrupted commits without preview preference writes or feature preparation.
- Second review and the independent completion audit found no remaining required issue. Both projects build; full suite passed 2,292/2,292 and focused HUD coverage passed 335/335, with no failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-phase5/phase5-full.trx` and `phase5-focused.trx` in the same directory (repository-relative). Diff checks are clean.
- No game was launched. Final documentation reconciliation and user-run in-game appearance/interaction acceptance remain in Phase 6; this completion does not claim that acceptance.
