- README usage and permanent HUD architecture documentation describe native controls, arbitrary grouping, permission-only modes, detach, global reset, persistence/migration, and effective default templates. Existing localized reset/group labels and native Fixed/Movable translations cover the implemented controls; no additional menu actions were added.
- Second source review and independent audit found no remaining required source/headless issue. The final canonical build passed without new warnings; focused HUD tests passed 335/335 and the full suite passed 2,292/2,292, with no failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-phase6/phase6-focused.trx` and `phase6-full.trx` (repository-relative). Final source edits only improve comments and regions; their build passed separately. Diff checks are clean.
- Corrective implementation passed second review and independent audit after resolving alignment collisions, free-drop collisions, and source-remainder reflow collisions. Direct-body movement uses the existing cancellable transaction and preserves native chrome/foreground priority. A pre-fix regression failed as expected; final rebuilt focused coverage passed 354/354 and full coverage passed 2,311/2,311, with zero failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-acceptance-fixes/focused-final.trx` and `full-final.trx` in the same directory. No index changes were made.
- Magnetic snapping corrections passed second review and independent audit: 16-pixel acquisition, 26-pixel release, retained target/member/side, alignment-zone hysteresis, grouping priority, and native-rounded guide placement. Final production/test build and focused coverage passed 370/370; full coverage passed 2,327/2,327, with no failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-magnetic-snapping/focused.trx` and `full.trx` in the same directory. Later test edits only add comments/regions. Existing overlap/Shift, cancellation, and persistence tests continue to pass. Updated interaction feel still requires user-run acceptance.
- Outward-growth placement passed second review and independent audit. Inserts/merges preserve the opposite destination edge and selected cross-axis anchor before native rounding/clamping. Native tests cover all sides, larger incoming content, nested insertion, Fixed targets, cancellation, preview/commit agreement, and restart reconstruction. Final rebuilt focused coverage passed 380/380 and full coverage passed 2,337/2,337, with no failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-outward-growth/outward-focused.trx` and `outward-full.trx` in the same directory. User-run acceptance remains pending.
- Container-only titlebars passed second review and independent audit. Member bodies retain direct dragging but never compose/render titlebars, expose chrome hit areas, or paint duplicate hover panels. Container menus and ordinary group handles remain available. Final build and focused coverage passed 380/380; full coverage passed 2,337/2,337, with zero failures or skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-group-titlebars/group-titlebars-focused.trx` and `group-titlebars-full.trx` in the same directory. User-run acceptance remains pending.
- Hidden-item editing passed second source/document review and independent audit. Session-owned compact proxies expose registered hidden/disabled/inapplicable/unprepared items through ordinary layout and controls, without fabricated readings or feature activation. Tests verify immediate cursor/global/session gating, transient missing-anchor fallback without preference writes, current registration identity, cached lettering and cleanup/failure isolation, separate feature/backdrop drawing, actual native placeholder dragging/detachment/grouping, commit, and cancellation. Final build and focused coverage passed 395/395; full coverage passed 2,352/2,352, zero failures/skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-hidden-edit/hidden-focused.trx` and `hidden-full.trx` in the same directory. In-game acceptance remains pending.
- Fixed native HUD boundaries passed second review and independent audit. Installed native IL/public API inspection verified hotbar/health/hunger visibility and the enabled temporal-gear hover element. Tests cover actual native bounds and offsets, fresh geometry, unavailable/ambiguous/spectator states, edge/center/exterior alignment without membership, fractional rounding, native collision rejection for free and expanded-group drops, Shift bypass, and unchanged native ownership/settings. Final build and focused coverage passed 425/425; full coverage passed 2,382/2,382, zero failures/skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-native-boundaries/native-focused.trx` and `native-full.trx` in the same directory. User-run acceptance remains pending.
- Screen-edge correction passed second review and independent audit. Player-positioned containers use actual viewport edges for guides, native clamping, and clipping; registered default padding remains unchanged. Tests cover all four edges at GUI scales 1, 1.5, and 2, offset viewports, preview/commit/reload agreement, and unclipped content within native integer-coordinate rounding. Build passed; focused coverage passed 429/429 and full coverage passed 2,386/2,386, zero failures/skips. Receipts: `artifacts/test-results/movable-hud-screen-edges/screen-edges-focused.trx` and `screen-edges-full.trx` in the same directory. User-run acceptance remains pending.
- User-run acceptance reported overlapping snaps and difficult titlebar targeting. Corrective work rejects overlapping drops unless Shift is held and adds direct indicator-body dragging; renewed live acceptance remains pending. No game was launched. The in-game acceptance tasks, final acceptance, and parent task remain unchecked; this is not completion of Phase 6.
## Final acceptance

- [ ] Every source-proposal requirement and resolved grouping decision is implemented and verified.
- [ ] Native coordinates and approved membership metadata restore a consistent layout while preserving feature ownership and unrelated settings.
- [ ] Required build/tests, documentation review, cleanup, independent audit, and user-run interaction acceptance are complete.
- [ ] Only after these gates pass, mark the parent movable-HUD task in `docs/project.todo` complete.
